<h3>Activity1 — teacher model</h3><p>Teacher hides a mystery quadrilateral from the previous lesson's cards. Class asks up to FIVE yes/no questions about SHAPE ATTRIBUTES, guesses then observes the original card.</p>
<h3>Activity2 — partner game</h3><ol><li>Partner A secretly chooses one actual quadrilateral card from previous lesson, conceals it in folder</li><li>Partner B asks UP TO FIVE YES/NO property questions to narrow down choices</li><li>Partner B guesses which source card it is</li><li>Partner A reveals selected card and explains truth of previous questions</li><li>Switch roles and play again</li></ol><p>Each pair uses cards from previous lesson and a folder. Counters may cover rejected candidates on the sheet. Focus on number/equality of sides and presence of right angles, not simply naming a type. Original card choice varies; teacher checks actual geometric truth.</p><p>Synthesis: compare source cards S, U and X by shared and contrasting attributes; original illustration card pixels are still unverified. Restricted teacher Cool-down not reproduced.</p></section>